## Stop embedding SQL quotes in exported R2RML column names

Context: Issue #144 — auto-generated R2RML wrapped every column in SQL
double-quotes. RDFLib then Turtle-escaped them (`rr:column "\"Label\""`,
`rr:template ".../{\"ID\"}"`), so Ontop looked up a column named `"Label"`
instead of `Label`. R2RML §7.2/`rr:column` is the bare name; §7.3 only
quotes non-plain identifiers inside templates.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/w3c/r2rml/R2RMLGenerator.py
   Emit raw names on `rr:column`; quote inside `rr:template` only when the
   name is not a plain SQL identifier.
2. src/back/core/w3c/r2rml/R2RMLParser.py
   Keep `_unquote_column` for older always-quoted exports.
3. tests/units/mapping/test_r2rml_generator.py
   Regression for #144 plus restored helper/template assertions.

Modified files:
- src/back/core/w3c/r2rml/R2RMLGenerator.py
- src/back/core/w3c/r2rml/R2RMLParser.py
- tests/units/mapping/test_r2rml_generator.py
